":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"combine"},{"type":"text","text":" methods. When you’ve finished feeding the hasher, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hash value can be retrieved by calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"finalize()"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var hasher = Hasher()","hasher.combine(23)","hasher.combine(\"Hello\")","let hashValue = hasher.finalize()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Within the execution of a Swift program, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hasher"},{"type":"text","text":" guarantees that finalizing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it will always produce the same hash value as long as it is fed the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same sequence of bytes. However, the underlying hash algorithm is designed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to exhibit avalanche effects: slight changes to the seed or the input byte"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence will typically produce drastic changes in the generated hash value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Do not save or otherwise reuse hash values across executions of your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"program. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hasher"},{"text":" is usually randomly seeded, which means it will return","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different values on every new execution of your program. The hash","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm implemented by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hasher"},{"text":" may itself change between any two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"versions of the standard library.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage"